# Responsive UI — non-negotiable (FleetOps)

User said this many times. Follow every UI create/change. Do not wait to be reminded.

## Hard rules

1. **Every page/change = both viewports.** Mobile (<1024) AND desktop (≥1024). Never ship mobile-only layout that stays skinny on desktop.
2. **Desktop must use screen space — balanced.** Full canvas width (no leftover gutters from `max-width: 28–36rem` + `margin-inline: auto`). 2-column when content fits. Do NOT starve form/content to feed a giant map.
3. **Maps stay medium side panels on desktop** (~35–40% width, ~18–20rem tall). Form / primary content gets majority width. Boxes (route, lists, cards) must be roomy — not tiny islands.
4. **Minimize needless desktop scroll** without crushing content. Cap secondary panels; keep primary actions readable.
5. **Mobile stays mobile.** Sticky CTAs, bottom-nav clearance, sheets — keep.
6. **Apply everywhere it is needed** — home, plan ride, request/trip detail, profile, list pages — not only the page just edited.
7. **Verify both before done.** Check ≤1023 and ≥1024. Rebuild Docker app after UI CSS/JSX changes.

## Breakpoints

| Token | px | Use |
|-------|-----|-----|
| `sm` | 640 | 2-col forms/KPIs |
| `md` | 768 | Table ↔ card list |
| `lg` | 1024 | Sidebar vs bottom nav; desktop splits start here |
| `xl` | 1280 | Dense KPI rows only |

Nav boundary = **`lg`**, not `md`.

## Patterns

- Detail pages: `ride-detail__desk` — main info left + map aside right
- Booking: form majority + map panel
- Home: hero 2-col (illus | where-to) + recent 2-col grid
- Profile: full width at lg (no 28rem cage)
- Tables: dual render (cards mobile, table `md+`)

## Ship checklist

- [ ] 375px: readable, tappable, no required horizontal scroll
- [ ] ≥1024px: full content width; roomy boxes; not phone column + empty gutters
- [ ] Desktop: form/content majority; maps medium side panels
- [ ] Same treatment on all related pages in the change, not one screen only
- [ ] Mobile patterns still work
